    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23462" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δάρατος</span></b> , ὁ, a
		Thessalian kind of <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bread,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Maced.
			</span></i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δράμις,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Seleuc.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				3.114b
			</span></i>: neut. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δάρατον</span></b> ,
				τό, prob. in <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				9(2).1202
			</span></i> (Coropa, <span class="entity">vi/v B.C.</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>unleavened bread,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				184
			</span></i>:—also fem. pl. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δαράται</span></b> , αἱ, <i>cakes</i>
			offered at marriage and registration ceremonies by a <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φρατρία,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Michel</u>
				995
			</span></i><i><span class="en">
				<u>A</u>
				5
			</span></i>, al. (Delph., <span class="entity">v/iv B.C.</span>).</div>
